      "notes": "repaired 2026-10-02 from the independent verification (docs/verification/2026-10-02-*) of the zai glm-5.3-flash transcription.\nRepairs: the cover-page instructions (problems p.1) and the mathematical hints (problems p.7) moved from the Problem 2 statement to paper.documentNotes; the Problem 2 and Problem 3 section headings and section texts restored in their printed places between the parts (statementAfter); the missing paragraphs \"In reality, …\" and \"Let the upper layer … completely absorb the thermal radiation of the Earth.\" restored (problems p.4); the duplicated block (8)–(17) in the Problem 2 solution and (18)–(31) in the Problem 3 solution removed; formula (20) restored as p = (ε/c)(c−V)/(c+V); the lead-in \"The area of this ring is written as\" before (41) restored; table formula (15) restored with T1; Problem 3 title and solution heading restored with \"Problem 3.\"; literal [figure …] markers (not printed) removed; invented captions of the Problem 1 figures removed; p2-sol-fig2 crop extended to include the Earth surface and t1; answers for 1.1–1.3 and 2.8–2.13 taken from the official solution; the false caveat \"Solution document not transcribed\" removed.\nProblems p.2: the figure label reads \"H = 3R\" while the text of Problem 1.1 says \"h = 3R\" — both kept as printed.\nSource errors kept verbatim: Wien paragraph \"λmax,,\" and \"rr0(λ,T)\"; \"φ(λ,T1),,\" in 2.7; \"K0(1+αt1),,\" before 2.9; \"c = 2.98·10^8 m/s\"; \"I = 1.00 μW/sm^2\"; 3.5 ends without a period; the hints print \"ln ln |x|\" and \"ln ln (1 + x)\" (Word export of ln); solution formula (6) of Problem 1.2 prints \"T/T\"; table formula (2) of Problem 1.3 prints \"dq = σdS\" (text: −σdS); typos \"emperature\", \"theupper\", \"evalulated\", \"obrained\", \"amd\", \"folows\" kept.\nProblem 2 grading table disagrees with the running solution: α = 0.031 K^-1 (text 0.014), K(t0) = 0.0757 and Δt1 = 2.65 °C (text 0.101 and 3.55 °C), Δt ≈ 2.84 °C (text 3.73 °C); both kept as printed, answers follow the running text and note the table.\nProblem 3 table formula (15) prints dM = (2Is/c)√(R²−x²)dx without the factor x, and table formula (36) prints M = FR (text M = −FR); kept as printed.\nNo per-part points are printed in the problems document; part points are null. The solutions print the per-part breakdown in the tables."
